# Slack API

Use Slack's Web API (base URL https://slack.com/api/) and Incoming Webhooks to send and read workspace messages. The bundled script scripts/slack_request.cjs performs one authenticated request so the HTTP code does not get rewritten every time. For multi-step work (resolve an ID, then act, then page through results) call the script once per step.

## Credentials and identifiers

- Bot tokens start with xoxb-; user tokens start with xoxp-. Prefer a bot token with the smallest scope set that still works.
- Read tokens from environment variables (SLACK_TOKEN, SLACK_BOT_TOKEN, SLACK_WEBHOOK_URL) or ask the user. Never hard-code a token in a file and never print a full token.
- Channel IDs start with C..., user IDs with U..., file IDs with F..., team IDs with T....
- A message timestamp (ts) such as 1700000000.123456 identifies a message and doubles as thread_ts for replies.

## Request helper

The helper needs Node.js 18+ and has no third-party dependencies. From the skill folder run:

    node scripts/slack_request.cjs --endpoint chat.postMessage --token "$SLACK_TOKEN" --payload '{"channel":"C1234567890","text":"Hello from a bot"}'

Send through an Incoming Webhook:

    node scripts/slack_request.cjs --webhook-url "$SLACK_WEBHOOK_URL" --payload '{"text":"Hello"}'

Flags: --endpoint (Web API method; default chat.postMessage), --token, --webhook-url, --payload, --payload-file. The payload may also be piped on stdin. On success the script prints Success: followed by trimmed JSON (webhooks answer with plain text). On failure it prints a concise reason and exits non-zero: 1 means usage, transport, or HTTP error; 2 means Slack answered ok:false; 75 means rate limited (retry after the Retry-After seconds Slack reports).

## Common operations

Post a message: chat.postMessage with a channel ID and text. Add link_names: true to turn plain @name and #channel text into links; pass blocks for rich layouts. Plain text is preferred over attachments.

Reply in a thread: set thread_ts to the parent message ts. The response carries reply_ts so later replies can chain.

Send an ephemeral message: chat.postEphemeral with channel, user, and text; only that user sees it.

Update or delete a message: chat.update or chat.delete with channel and ts.

Resolve a channel name to an ID: conversations.list with types "public_channel,private_channel" and limit 1000, paging with cursor from response_metadata.next_cursor until the name matches. Needs channels:read and groups:read. When the app is already in the channel, conversations.info with the channel ID is cheaper.

Find a user: users.lookupByEmail with email (scope users:read.email), or page users.list with limit 1000. User IDs are stable; emails and display names are not.

Read history: conversations.history with channel and limit, plus optional oldest and latest (Unix seconds) to bound the window. Messages carry ts, user, text, and subtype for special kinds; page with next_cursor.

React to a message: reactions.add with channel, name (no colons), and timestamp; reactions.remove works the same way.

Search messages: search.messages with query (scope search:read).

Upload a file: files.upload is deprecated. Call files.getUploadURLExternal with filename and length to get upload_url and file_id, POST the raw bytes to upload_url (for example curl -F file=@report.csv "upload_url"), then call files.completeUploadExternal with files: [{"id":"F...","title":"report.csv"}]. Scope: files:write.

Open a modal: views.open with a view object and the trigger_id from an interaction.

## Message formatting

Slack uses mrkdwn: *bold*, _italic_, ~strikethrough~, and code spans wrapped in the single back-tick character. Mention a user with <@U123...>, reference a channel with <#C123...>, and hyperlink with <https://example.com|link text>. Set link_names: true to link plain @name and #channel text.

## Responses and errors

Web API responses set ok to true or false. Treat ok:false as a failure and surface the error string. Common errors:

- invalid_auth, not_authed, account_inactive: token wrong, revoked, or from a deleted app; ask for a fresh one.
- missing_scope: add the scope to the app and reinstall it in the workspace.
- channel_not_found: use the channel ID, not the name, and confirm the app is in the channel.
- not_in_channel: join public channels with conversations.join or ask an admin to invite the app.
- is_archived: pick a channel that is not archived.
- msg_too_long: text is limited to 40,000 characters; split the message or trim it.
- rate_limited: HTTP 429 with Retry-After; wait that many seconds and retry (the helper exits 75).

Pagination: methods return up to 100 to 1000 records per page (see the method docs) plus response_metadata.next_cursor. Keep paging while the cursor is non-empty and stop once the user's requested volume is reached.

Rate limits: roughly one request per second per method. Delay briefly between calls in a loop and always honor Retry-After on 429.

## Typical multi-step flow

1. Resolve targets first: look up channel and user IDs once and reuse them.
2. Perform the action with IDs.
3. Page only as far as needed and summarize counts instead of dumping full lists.
4. Report what was done: channel, message ts, and any failures.

## Scope checklist

chat:write to send, update, and delete messages; chat:write.customize for bot name and icon overrides; channels:read and groups:read for conversation metadata; im:read and mpim:read for DM and group history; users:read and users:read.email for member lookup; reactions:write; files:write for uploads; search:read for search.messages; incoming-webhook when using a webhook URL.
`;

const helperSource = String.raw`#!/usr/bin/env node
/*
 * slack_request.cjs - one Slack request with LLM-friendly output.
 * Bundled with the slack-api skill. Requires Node.js 18+ (global fetch).
 * No third-party dependencies.
 *
 * Usage:
 *   node scripts/slack_request.cjs --endpoint chat.postMessage \
 *       --token "$SLACK_TOKEN" \
 *       --payload '{"channel":"C1234567890","text":"Hello"}'
 *   node scripts/slack_request.cjs --webhook-url "$SLACK_WEBHOOK_URL" \
 *       --payload '{"text":"Hello"}'
 *   node scripts/slack_request.cjs --endpoint conversations.history \
 *       --token "$SLACK_TOKEN" --payload-file history.json
 *   echo '{"channel":"C1234567890","text":"hi"}' | node scripts/slack_request.cjs \
 *       --token "$SLACK_TOKEN"
 *
 * Exit codes: 0 success; 1 usage/transport/HTTP error; 2 Slack API error
 * (ok:false); 75 rate limited (retry after the reported Retry-After seconds).
 */
'use strict';

const fs = require('fs');
const path = require('path');

function usageError(message) {
  process.stderr.write('Error: ' + message + '\n');
  process.stderr.write('Usage: node slack_request.cjs (--token TOKEN | --webhook-url URL) [--endpoint METHOD] (--payload JSON | --payload-file FILE | stdin)\n');
  process.exit(1);
}

function parseArgs(argv) {
  const options = { endpoint: 'chat.postMessage', payload: null, payloadFile: null, token: null, webhookUrl: null };
  for (let i = 0; i < argv.length; i = i + 1) {
    const flag = argv[i];
    const nextValue = function () {
      i = i + 1;
      if (i >= argv.length) usageError('Missing value for ' + flag);
      return argv[i];
    };
    if (flag === '--endpoint') options.endpoint = nextValue();
    else if (flag === '--token') options.token = nextValue();
    else if (flag === '--webhook-url') options.webhookUrl = nextValue();
    else if (flag === '--payload') options.payload = nextValue();
    else if (flag === '--payload-file') options.payloadFile = nextValue();
    else usageError('Unknown flag: ' + flag);
  }
  return options;
}

function readPayload(options) {
  if (options.payload !== null && options.payloadFile !== null) {
    usageError('Use either --payload or --payload-file, not both');
  }
  let raw = options.payload;
  if (options.payloadFile !== null) {
    try {
      raw = fs.readFileSync(path.resolve(options.payloadFile), 'utf8');
    } catch (error) {
      usageError('Could not read payload file: ' + error.message);
    }
  } else if (raw === null) {
    if (process.stdin.isTTY) {
      usageError('No payload provided; pass --payload JSON, --payload-file FILE, or pipe JSON on stdin');
    }
    try {
      raw = fs.readFileSync(0, 'utf8');
    } catch (error) {
      usageError('Could not read stdin payload: ' + error.message);
    }
  }
  if (raw === null || raw.trim().length === 0) usageError('Payload is empty');
  try {
    return JSON.parse(raw);
  } catch (error) {
    usageError('Payload is not valid JSON: ' + error.message);
  }
}

function trimOutput(text, maxLines, maxChars) {
  if (maxLines === undefined) maxLines = 60;
  if (maxChars === undefined) maxChars = 6000;
  const allLines = String(text).split('\n');
  let result = allLines.slice(0, maxLines).join('\n');
  if (allLines.length > maxLines) {
    result = result + '\n... (' + (allLines.length - maxLines) + ' more lines)';
  }
  if (result.length > maxChars) {
    result = result.slice(0, maxChars) + '\n... (output truncated)';
  }
  return result;
}

async function main() {
  const options = parseArgs(process.argv.slice(2));
  const token = options.token || process.env.SLACK_TOKEN || process.env.SLACK_BOT_TOKEN || '';
  const webhookUrl = options.webhookUrl || process.env.SLACK_WEBHOOK_URL || '';

  if (token === '' && webhookUrl === '') {
    usageError('Provide --token (or set SLACK_TOKEN) for the Web API, or --webhook-url (or set SLACK_WEBHOOK_URL) for a webhook');
  }
  if (token !== '' && webhookUrl !== '') {
    usageError('Provide either a webhook URL or a token, not both');
  }

  const payload = readPayload(options);
  const url = webhookUrl !== '' ? webhookUrl : 'https://slack.com/api/' + options.endpoint;
  const headers = { 'Content-Type': 'application/json; charset=utf-8' };
  if (token !== '') headers.Authorization = 'Bearer ' + token;

  let response;
  try {
    response = await fetch(url, { method: 'POST', headers: headers, body: JSON.stringify(payload) });
  } catch (error) {
    process.stderr.write('Error: could not reach Slack: ' + error.message + '\n');
    process.exit(1);
  }

  if (response.status === 429) {
    const retryAfter = Number(response.headers.get('retry-after') || '1') || 1;
    process.stderr.write('Error: rate limited by Slack (HTTP 429); retry after ' + retryAfter + ' seconds\n');
    process.exit(75);
  }

  const text = await response.text();
  if (!response.ok) {
    process.stderr.write('Error: Slack HTTP ' + response.status + ' ' + response.statusText + '\n' + trimOutput(text, 10) + '\n');
    process.exit(1);
  }

  let data = null;
  try {
    data = JSON.parse(text);
  } catch (error) {
    data = null; // Incoming Webhooks respond with plain text
  }

  if (data !== null && data.ok === false) {
    let message = 'Error: Slack API error: ' + String(data.error);
    if (data.response_metadata && Array.isArray(data.response_metadata.messages) && data.response_metadata.messages.length > 0) {
      message = message + ' (' + data.response_metadata.messages.join('; ') + ')';
    }
    process.stderr.write(message + '\n');
    process.exit(2);
  }

  if (data === null) {
    process.stdout.write('Success: ' + trimOutput(text, 10) + '\n');
  } else {
    process.stdout.write('Success: ' + trimOutput(JSON.stringify(data, null, 2)) + '\n');
  }
}

main().catch(function (error) {
  process.stderr.write('Error: unexpected failure: ' + (error && error.message ? error.message : String(error)) + '\n');
  process.exit(1);
});
`;

function writeSkillFiles() {
  fs.mkdirSync(path.join(SKILL_DIR, 'scripts'), { recursive: true });
  fs.writeFileSync(SKILL_MD_PATH, skillMarkdown, 'utf8');
  fs.writeFileSync(HELPER_PATH, helperSource, 'utf8');
}

function validateArtifacts() {
  const problems = [];
  const md = fs.readFileSync(SKILL_MD_PATH, 'utf8');
  const helper = fs.readFileSync(HELPER_PATH, 'utf8');

  if (md.indexOf('name: ' + SKILL_NAME) === -1) {
    problems.push('SKILL.md frontmatter is missing name: ' + SKILL_NAME);
  }
  if (md.indexOf('description:') === -1) {
    problems.push('SKILL.md frontmatter is missing description');
  }
  if (md.indexOf('scripts/slack_request.cjs') === -1) {
    problems.push('SKILL.md does not reference the bundled helper script');
  }
  if (md.indexOf('TODO') !== -1) {
    problems.push('SKILL.md still contains TODO markers');
  }
  if (md.trim().length === 0) {
    problems.push('SKILL.md is empty');
  }
  if (helper.indexOf('#!/usr/bin/env node') !== 0) {
    problems.push('helper script is missing its shebang');
  }
  if (helper.indexOf('https://slack.com/api/') === -1) {
    problems.push('helper script does not target the Slack Web API');
  }
  if (helper.trim().length === 0) {
    problems.push('helper script is empty');
  }
  return problems;
}

function main() {
  writeSkillFiles();

  const mdBytes = fs.statSync(SKILL_MD_PATH).size;
  const helperBytes = fs.statSync(HELPER_PATH).size;

  const problems = validateArtifacts();
  if (problems.length > 0) {
    for (let p = 0; p < problems.length; p = p + 1) {
      process.stderr.write('Validation problem: ' + problems[p] + '\n');
    }
    process.exitCode = 1;
    return;
  }

  process.stdout.write('Created skill folder: ' + SKILL_DIR + '\n');
  process.stdout.write('  SKILL.md (' + mdBytes + ' bytes)\n');
  process.stdout.write('  scripts/slack_request.cjs (' + helperBytes + ' bytes)\n');
  process.stdout.write('Success: the ' + SKILL_NAME + ' skill was created and validated.\n');
}

main();

